  https://github.com/sizhet/Principle-Intelligence-and-Open-Structural-Learning

url: >-
  https://github.com/sizhet/Principle-Intelligence-and-Open-Structural-Learning

license: Apache-2.0

abstract: >-
  Principle Intelligence and Open Structural Learning develops a structural
  learning framework for extracting reusable Principles from sparse and
  differential evidence, validating them through supporting evidence,
  counter-evidence, and Two-Way CCC, and evolving them as evidence-bound
  Knowledge Roots. The framework introduces the Open-LHS Principle, in which
  the left-hand side of a Principle is not restricted to a permanently
  predefined symbolic vocabulary. Existing, retrieved, composed, or
  runtime-generated intelligence structures—including observations,
  differences, metrics, trajectories, CCCs, Principles, counter-evidence,
  triggers, policies, PIRPs, PIRUs, and other typed structural objects—may
  participate in Principle formation and evaluation. When required structure
  is missing, runtime structural generation may search, retrieve, compose,
  generate, unfold, or delegate the creation of a compatible structure and
  bind it into active reasoning. The repository further connects Principle
  Intelligence with Context-Condition-Consequence structures, Two-Way
  validation, Counter-Evidence Delta Intelligence, Universal Typing and
  Naming, Portable Intelligence Runtime Pieces and Units, Collective
  Learning, and Open-Ended Structural Growth. The central research
  proposition is that reusable intelligence structures can sometimes be
  extracted from experience, preserved with evidence and provenance,
  revised through counter-evidence, externalized for portable reuse, and
  incorporated into an extensible structural vocabulary for future
  intelligence.

